e same applies to `outputStream.add()`. Negated globs are never watched.\n- **Matching:** `processEvent` now calls a new `findGlob` helper, which returns the positive glob matching the file or one of its parent directories (so `watch(dir)` still includes its contents), and rejects files excluded by a negated glob. Events that match nothing are dropped silently.\n- **Removed:** the \"Watched unexpected path… likely a bug\" log block. Under chokidar 4 a non-matching event is a normal case inside a watched parent directory, so that message would fire constantly. This is a behaviour change for anyone who relied on that message, and it also removed the `originalGlobs` variable it used.\n\n**Lint:** `npm test` runs `xo` first, so I also adjusted five lint issues in the new code (comment capitalisation and wrapping function references in arrow functions).\n\nI didn't touch `package.json`, lockfiles, `node_modules`, or any test files. `test/fixtures` is clean after the run.","ttft_ms":1009,"type":"result","duration_ms":65007,"uuid":"9b86c610-d60e-4063-8e5e-71def9bb8afa","begun_message_ids":["msg_011ChMS6fXwLC4Sf5gUxWtdT","msg_011ChMS6kQdtutt7465kY9ra","msg_011ChMS6pm4jTi87U6e3PvhF","msg_011ChMS75JvtTiQeD8QbCcrY","msg_011ChMS8mD3tzvTk5WGrd7n8","msg_011ChMSA3cZZUg7p8nHCijHu","msg_011ChMSAPd6JWdbhNmF94kzr","msg_011ChMSAUxKGNpBtBeUQM4hE","msg_011ChMSAkr2eutGsseUnRWxP","msg_011ChMSB8Eu9Wo4oxD6dYvmn","msg_011ChMSBFJZAVyANAG73rX7s"],"ttft_stream_ms":999,"time_to_request_ms":281,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":42,"system_prompt":9,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":25,"input_hooks":5,"conversation_append":2,"transcript_persist":20,"tool_pool_refresh":3,"init_message":20,"init_frame_send":22,"engine_pickup":18,"loop_entry":38,"message_prep":12,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":5,"request_announcements":15,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":9,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":12,"request_build":14},"turn_start_resume_kind":"n